  "historyNote": "#8405, eff 8-2-05 (formerly Saf-C 1801.24); ss by #10523, eff 2-18-14, EXPIRED: 2-18-24 New. #13963, EMERGENCY RULE, eff 5-13-24; ss by #14100, eff 10-18-24, EXPIRES: 10-18-34",
  "inScheme": "https://granitestate.github.io/rules/scheme",
  "notation": "Saf-C 1802.28",
  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c1800.html",
  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 1802.28 Tank vehicle",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 1802.28 “Tank vehicle” means any commercial motor vehicle that is designed to transport any liquid or gaseous materials within a tank or tanks having an individual rated capacity of more than 119 gallons and an aggregate rated capacity of 1,000 gallons or more that is either permanently or temporarily attached to the vehicle or the chassis. The term does not include a commercial motor vehicle transporting an\n\nempty storage container tank, not designed for transportation, with a rated capacity of 1,000 gallons or more that is temporarily attached to a flatbed trailer.\n\nSource. #8405, eff 8-2-05 (formerly Saf-C 1801.24); ss by #10523, eff 2-18-14, EXPIRED: 2-18-24\n\nNew. #13963, EMERGENCY RULE, eff 5-13-24; ss by #14100, eff 10-18-24, EXPIRES: 10-18-34",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c1800.html"
